    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, labelled by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 e.g. a registration date of 2026-08-21 \u2192 **FY27**).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` field (`FY<YY>`) to the `Owner` schema, and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reference the fiscal year / elapsed fiscal years.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Added `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 the shared fiscal-year helper (month \u2265 July \u2192 year+1, else year).\n- `membershipNumberFor(...)` now uses the fiscal year's last two digits instead of the calendar year, so the `-M<YY>` segment matches `fiscalYear`.\n- Renamed the tenure threshold to `TENURE_POINTS_THRESHOLD_FISCAL_YEARS = 1` and replaced `tenureInDays` (a 365-day window via `ChronoUnit`) with `tenureInFiscalYears`, counting elapsed 1-July boundaries between registration date and now. A freshly created owner still has zero tenure, so tenure points still never apply on create (Cp39/Cp40 stay green).\n- Swapped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import for `Month`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `deriveFiscalYear(Owner)` (derived on read from the stored, business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`) and wired it via `@Mapping(target = \"fiscalYear\", ...)`, consistent with the other derived fields.\n\nThe controller and mapper use the identical fiscal-year formula, guaranteeing the membership number's year segment always matches the returned `fiscalYear` (verified by Cp14, Cp48, and the full 60-test suite).",
